{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1335863-ronin-nation-w20-idea","id":1335863,"title":"Ronin Nation (W20 Idea)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-15T04:26:06-07:00","id":1335863,"title":"Ronin Nation (W20 Idea)","content":"one of the things it Suggests as a major potential problem in W20<br /> <br /> is the possible birth of a Ronin Nation Which gives all the Convewniences of the Garou nation but none of the responsibleetys<br /> <br /> How do you think such a thing would look<br /> <br /> it says many Garou would see the possible creation of such a thing as a threat and attack the possiblety of its emergance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T17:50:22-07:00","id":1335967,"title":"","content":"As a political organization, I don't think a 'Ronin Nation' or 'Ghost Wolf Nation' has much of a chance of becoming a major rival or alternative to the Garou Nation, purely for the reason that it's unlikely that garou who define themselves by independence and desperation from the GN are unlikely to be interested in creating a new social hierarchy as opposed to the old one.<br /> <br /> However, as a cultural movement, I can see the idea of a Robin Nation being terrifying the the elders of the Garou Nation. If there were to be a rising sense of apathy and nihilism regarding the Nation's chances of ever truly defeating the Wyrm or averting the Apocalypse, it is not hard to imagine that a new generation of garou may see young members deciding left and right that they don't want to devote their lives to a religious war without end which they were drafted into without warning or choice, simply by the merit of their birth.<br /> <br /> I don't see a Ghost Wolf Nation rising to challenge the Garou Nation politically but as a cultural movement? I can easily imagine the leadership of the Nation becoming horrified as to the state of the battle and the impending Apocalypse as lost clubs and disaffected cliath left the conflict to live their own lives as best they could. <br /> <br /> That would be what terrifies the garou elders most I think. Not a political schism that threatens a civil war, which would give a chance for the warrior nation to prove its legitimacy with blood red tooth and claw. No, instead, a Nation that watches itself begin to slowly evaporate as its recruits grow disillusioned and with a harano-like nihilism become ready to fiddle while Gaia burns. That I think is the image that terrifies them. A world where the Garou no longer care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T01:48:56-07:00","id":1336003,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd guess it would be a move torwards 'Forsaken' in a sense. I mean, 'WoD: Outcasts' gave mechanics for corruption and basically a VtM humanity decline in the WtA setting. Even with no mechanics given in other sources it was this dread that hung over Ronin all the time - slowly loosing themselves because of a lack of ties to to a community, religing, ethics and what not.<br /> <br /> If now Prides of Ronin become more common, forming their own localized mini-cultures, they could probably shake of the threat of corruption by giving them their own set of rules and moral standards as well as Rites and ceremonies to spiritually tie them to these morals, warding of any corruption.<br /> <br /> So, if a &quot;Ghost Wolf Nation&quot; is a catch all term for local communities of Ronin, not really having much in common besides their wish not to adhere to the standards of the Garou Nation, then I think it could be a nice addition to the Setting. However, I feel that granting them as a playable option would weaken the Setting as a whole, for it would allow players to play without a lot of core themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T18:34:06-07:00","id":1336134,"title":"","content":"...Ronin are defined as being outside the spirit pact that grants most of the benefits of the Garou Nation. How are they going to preserve any of the conveniences of the concordat if they give up that one, by which Garou can readily gain Gifts and get spirits to vet their status?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T06:53:38-07:00","id":1336197,"title":"","content":"Garou back in the day didn't really have the numbers to have a Ronin Nation, but they loosened the numbers in W20 (not always a good thing because its hard to hammer in a concrete setting and the endangered species angle when they treat population cheaply).<br /> <br /> But oddly enough I added Ghost Wolves as part of my Headcanon when W20 came out. In my setting the Amazon War resulted in a lot of Kinfolk being born in South America, and a lot of Garou being born without kinfetches. They pretty much formed as the tribe with even less responsibility then joining the Bonegnawers (which before virtually anyone could join, and while a lot took up responsibilities they still had a lot of loafers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}